  "text": "That sounds like a wonderful idea! A classic breakfast omelette is a great, simple, and comforting dish to surprise your mom with. Here's a step-by-step guide to making a classic breakfast omelette:\n\n### \ud83c\udf73 Classic Breakfast Omelette Recipe\n\n#### **Ingredients:**\n- 2 large eggs\n- 2 tablespoons milk (or cream for a richer flavor)\n- A pinch of salt and pepper\n- 1/4 teaspoon butter or oil\n- Optional fillings: cheese, ham, vegetables (like spinach, mushrooms, or bell peppers)\n\n#### **Instructions:**\n\n1. **Whisk the eggs:** In a bowl, crack the eggs and add the milk, salt, and pepper. Whisk until the mixture is smooth and well combined.\n\n2. **Heat the pan:** Place a non-stick skillet over medium heat and add the butter or oil. Let it melt and coat the bottom of the pan.\n\n3. **Cook the eggs:** Pour the egg mixture into the pan. Let it sit for a few seconds until the edges begin to set.\n\n4. **Gently fold:** Use a spatula to carefully fold the omelette in half. If you're using fillings, add them now to one half of the omelette.\n\n5. **Cook the other side:** Let the omelette cook for another 1\u20132 minutes, or until the top is set and golden.\n\n6. **Serve:** Slide the omelette onto a plate and serve warm.\n\n#### **Tips for a Perfect Omelette:**\n- Use a non-stick pan to prevent sticking.\n- Don't stir the eggs; let them cook slowly.\n- For fluffier eggs, you can also whisk in a little air with a fork before cooking.\n- If you don't have fillings, you can still enjoy a simple, classic omelette with just cheese and herbs.\n\n#### \ud83c\udf81 Surprise Touch:\n- You can add a small card or a handwritten note to make it even more special.\n- Consider pairing it with toast, fruit, or coffee for a complete breakfast.\n\nI hope your mom enjoys this delicious and thoughtful breakfast! Let me know if you'd like any variations or help with other recipes. What kind of fillings do you think would be a good surprise?",
